      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CATWALK ICON (4) was not suited to a heavy track, and a very passive ride late at Ballarat last start when finishing third as the favourite in a 5-horse field. She will be peaking for a similarly small field here, but this time will have Harry Coffey in the saddle, which will make a big difference. Follow your money. SHALAILED (3) won his penultimate start at Echuca, and then led up to only be nabbed late for second at Swan Hill nearly 3 weeks ago. He has a superior gate this time, and can take them all the way. RACEY CASEY (9) is deep into her prep, and has been holding her form strongly since winning at Hamilton in September. She was run down off the top at Warrnambool 9-days ago over 1400m, and may try similar front running tactics here. Dean Yendall sticks with her, and so do we. GREATHAM BOY (2) did a lot wrong as the favourite after missing the kick at Albury last start. He is worth another chance here.",
